# Kron Project Conventions

Cursor-native companion to [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Read both before writing code.

## Tech stack (locked)

- Go 1.27 for core CLI (`cmd/kron/`, `internal/`)
- cobra for CLI parsing
- TOML for config (`BurntSushi/toml`)
- YAML for frontmatter (`gopkg.in/yaml.v3`)
- testify for test assertions
- TypeScript only when GUI phase begins

## Repo layout

```
cmd/kron/        ← thin CLI entry, wiring only
internal/model/  ← domain types
internal/store/  ← file I/O
internal/parser/ ← input parsing
internal/cli/    ← cobra command implementations
docs/            ← design notes
.cursor/skills/  ← detailed style rules (auto-loaded)
.cursor/rules/   ← Cursor-native rule format (this file)
```

**Business logic goes in `internal/`. Never in `cmd/`.**

## Workflow

1. Read `docs/article.md` and `docs/requirements.md` before coding.
2. Verify the relevant skill (`go-style` or `ts-style`) is loaded.
3. Write tests for any new exported function in the same change.
4. Run before committing: `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l .`, `go test ./...`.

## Off-limits without explicit human approval

- Adding new top-level dependencies (`go.mod` `require` block)
- Modifying the Go version in `go.mod`
- Renaming or moving packages
- Reflection or `go generate` (must have a `// why` comment)
- Force-pushes, history rewrites on shared branches
- Changing the `.kron/intents/*.md` frontmatter schema

## Skills (auto-loaded per language)

- `go-style` → see [SKILL.md](../skills/go-style/SKILL.md)
- `ts-style` → see [SKILL.md](../skills/ts-style/SKILL.md)

When in doubt: pick the more conservative / explicit option. Ask before adding deps or changing schemas.
